{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_gx4h5gpqmgadniq4kt4n3qwsjxozm777p6re2fisutrdxld2clbq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. Everything passes; here's the summary.\n\n## Result: the Rust translation is byte-identical to the C — **zero divergences found**, no fixes to `src/lib.rs` were needed.\n\n### Phase A — surface mapped (3 artifacts in the crate root)\n\n| artifact | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | All 3 C exports (`get_os_arch`, `w_regexec`, `parse_uname_string`) + verified ABI facts (`REG_EXTENDED=1`, `sizeof(regoff_t)=4`, `regmatch_t=8`, `regex_t=64`, `os_data`=9×`char*`) |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **40 rows**, mechanically grepped from every `return 0` / `return NULL` / bare `return` / untouched-`os_data`-member path |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **47 rows** — the pruned cross-product of the axes the C branches on (B1/B2/B3 markers × C1–C4 sub-branches × D1–D6 version shapes × 12 archs × `nmatch` sweep × `os_data` state) |\n\n**Build configs:** `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` and `CMakeLists.txt` has no `option()`/`#ifdef` → exactly **one** feature combination. I additionally verified both cargo **profiles**, since `dev` has overflow-checks/debug-assertions and `release` has `panic = \"abort\"`.\n\n### Phases B/C — 97 differential tests, all via `libloading` on both `.so`s\nNever calls Rust directly, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrappers are under test. Each case compares: return value, all 9 `os_data` members (poisoned with `0x00` **and** `0xAA` so untouched-vs-`NULL`-vs-`\"\"` are distinguishable), every produced heap string, the full `pmatch` array, and **every byte of a guard-padded `uname` buffer** — which captures the C's out-of-bounds `*(str_tmp + strlen(str_tmp) - 1) = '\\0'` write, faithfully reproduced by the Rust.\n\nBeyond the tables: byte-exact `stderr` comparison for the `regcomp`-failure diagnostic (incl. patterns containing `%s`/`%%`/non-UTF8), and **crash parity** via `fork()`+`waitpid` for the 3 NULL-deref paths, with negative controls proving the harness distinguishes a crash from a clean return.\n\nTwo bugs were in **my tests**, not the Rust: `)` and `a{,}` actually *compile* under glibc ERE (I'd assumed rejection), and `pmatch == NULL` with `nmatch > 0` segfaults inside glibc `regexec` — that turned out to be a genuine error-surface row I'd missed, now **ERRORS.md row 40**.\n\n### Phase D — completion gate\n- `nm -D` diff: **empty in both directions**, both profiles (no missing, no extra, no unresolved project symbols).\n- Only one C translation unit exists (`src/lib.c`) and all 3 of its non-`static` functions were already translated — no module was skipped, so nothing needed new translation.\n- `./verify.sh` automates the whole gate: `ALL CHECKS PASSED` (97 passed / 0 failed in both `dev` and `release`).\n\nI also ran a deep fuzz campaign (`HARVEST_FUZZ_ITERS=1000000`) — **~4.2 million** additional randomized differential cases across all three entry points and the composed pipeline, in both profiles, with no divergence.\n\nOne note for reuse: `cargo test --test <name>` doesn't always materialise the `cdylib`, so the harness now auto-builds both `.so`s on demand (disable with `HARVEST_NO_AUTOBUILD=1`). `c_src/` sources are untouched — only the `build/` directory was added, as the task's own build instructions require."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":960,"cache_read_input_tokens":165961,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":960,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4da87fc6-9527-451e-a988-a5d3a3a9961a","uuid":"936fa929-b904-41b8-993f-3446f77d6882","timestamp":"2026-08-20T12:52:02.424Z"}
